@startuml
title Bracelet ESP-NOW Packet Flow

participant "Bracelet ESP32-C3" as Bracelet
participant "Station ESP32" as Station

Bracelet -> Bracelet : Read MAC as 6-byte device_id
Bracelet -> Bracelet : Initialize ESP-NOW in WiFi STA mode
Bracelet -> Bracelet : Hop ESP-NOW channels 1..13\nuntil station_control is heard
Bracelet -> Station : bracelet_status broadcast\nprotocol=2, type=1, role=bracelet\nstate, latest energy, retained movement event,\nbattery, fault, flags, vibration_ack_id

loop every 200 ms
  Bracelet -> Bracelet : retain newest threshold event\nfor at most 10 seconds
  Bracelet -> Station : latest energy plus unacknowledged event\nid, uptime, energy and valid_ms
end

Station -> Bracelet : station_control optional\nprotocol=2, type=2, role=station\nstation_state, revision, movement acknowledgement,\nvibration_request, vibration_request_id, profile
Bracelet -> Station : bracelet_status reply delayed by 100 ms
Station -> Station : derive event age from bracelet uptime\nand mute for 10 seconds minus age
Bracelet -> Bracelet : start motor for a new vibration request id
Bracelet -> Station : force status with matching vibration_ack_id
note right of Bracelet
  station_state values mirror the station enum:
  idle=0, armed=1, ringing=2,
  validating_activity=3, stopped=4, fault=5.
  A received station_control locks the bracelet
  onto that ESP-NOW channel for 15 seconds.
end note

note right of Station
Station remains the alarm authority.
Bracelet energy above threshold mutes alarm
audio for 10 seconds during the station-owned
10-minute activity window.
end note

@enduml
